1
00:00:01,199 --> 00:00:03,240
Cent #1867.

2
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,220
Every physical coin joins two things:

3
00:00:09,660 --> 00:00:10,900
metal and stamp.

4
00:00:12,140 --> 00:00:12,960
In a copper cent,

5
00:00:13,160 --> 00:00:15,480
the coin's face and its metal had come apart.

6
00:00:16,179 --> 00:00:18,839
Hoarding such coins, Chang said in 2017,

7
00:00:19,579 --> 00:00:22,079
was like "buying 1.7 cents of copper

8
00:00:22,179 --> 00:00:24,660
for one cent and it's still worth one cent."

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,239
Chang took the two apart.

10
00:00:27,879 --> 00:00:30,539
He inscribed the image of each obverse on Bitcoin,

11
00:00:30,679 --> 00:00:32,859
and had the physical coins melted and cast

12
00:00:32,899 --> 00:00:35,399
into one block, CENTS Block Copper.

13
00:00:36,560 --> 00:00:39,000
Boris Groys describes two ways of archiving:

14
00:00:39,359 --> 00:00:40,700
"the object without an aura"

15
00:00:41,039 --> 00:00:42,960
and "the aura without an object."

16
00:00:43,820 --> 00:00:44,939
CENTS keeps both.

17
00:00:46,179 --> 00:00:48,560
In the image of Cent #1867,

18
00:00:48,799 --> 00:00:50,159
the copper's own chemistry

19
00:00:50,320 --> 00:00:52,079
spreads over the stamp of the state.

20
00:00:53,259 --> 00:00:55,719
A dark band of Significant Obsidian crosses

21
00:00:55,759 --> 00:00:58,340
the upper left, over the motto and Lincoln's head.

22
00:00:59,479 --> 00:01:01,859
Green patches of Significant Verdigris gather

23
00:01:01,899 --> 00:01:04,480
on his cheek, behind his head and at his collar.

24
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:07,379
A third trait came from outside:

25
00:01:07,760 --> 00:01:09,819
Contaminated, Alien Secretion.

26
00:01:10,239 --> 00:01:12,640
In the Traits Atlas, Alien Secretion names

27
00:01:12,859 --> 00:01:15,760
"unidentifiable translucent or greenish films".

28
00:01:16,700 --> 00:01:18,920
Compare it to Cent #4421,

29
00:01:19,260 --> 00:01:22,079
also dated 1964 and close to mint state.

30
00:01:23,219 --> 00:01:25,879
A cent held at one cent by the state became

31
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:27,560
a Cent whose value and meaning

32
00:01:27,599 --> 00:01:29,159
are set, and set again,

33
00:01:29,319 --> 00:01:31,920
by the people who keep, read and exchange it.

34
00:01:33,379 --> 00:01:36,540
Cent #1867, a great Cent.

35
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:40,799
Find out more about the project on cents.gallery,

36
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,299
and explore the traits on cents.vision.
